B = [
('Meissen','Europe','18th century','ceramics','In the style of Meissen, lustrous white hard-paste porcelain with a glassy, flawless glaze and delicate, thin, translucent surfaces. Hand-painted scattered sprays of flowers, small insects and colourful birds float on the white ground, with fine feathery brushwork and tiny enamel details. Rich cobalt blue and deep gold bands, lacy gilded borders and raised moulded basket-weave or scrolling relief frame the painting. Palette is white, cobalt, rose pink, leaf green, lemon yellow and burnished gold. Ornament is rococo, curving, symmetrical and finely crafted. Small crossed blue sword marks and tidy, spidery lettering appear as a discreet maker emblem.'),
('Lalique','Europe','1920s','glass','In the style of Lalique, French Art Deco moulded glass that is frosted, satin-matte and crystal clear in the same piece. Deeply relief-moulded motifs of birds, fish, dragonflies, thistles, grapes and stylised female figures repeat in rhythmic bands with sharp, stepped, geometric edges. Milky opalescent glass glows pale blue against warm amber, and tints of sapphire, emerald, black and smoky grey add depth. Polished highlights contrast with velvety acid-etched textures. Lettering is slim, elegant, upright capitals, often etched small at the base as a signature. Luxurious, sculptural, light-catching and refined.'),
('Georg Jensen','Europe','1900s-1950s','silverware','In the style of Georg Jensen, Danish sterling silver shaped into soft, organic, sculptural forms. Surfaces are gently hammered or smoothly polished, with a cool, mirror-like glow that darkens to grey in recesses. Ornament draws on nature through rounded grapes, flowing vines, buds, leaves, daisies and abstract curving ribbons, set with the occasional cabochon of amber, moonstone or blue stone. Shapes are plump, rounded, flowing and balanced, later giving way to pure modernist smoothness with clean, tapering geometry. Palette is silver, soft grey, honey amber and white enamel. Lettering is tiny, neat and stamped, as a hallmark.'),
('Iittala','Europe','1950s','glass','In the style of Iittala, Finnish Scandinavian design with calm, honest, timeless simplicity. Forms are organic and fluid, with undulating leaf-like curves, free-form wavy outlines inspired by lake shores, and pure cylindrical or softly rounded geometry. Materials are clear, tinted and frosted glass, smooth glazed ceramic and a few matte finishes. Palette is cool and clear with ice blue, aqua, smoky grey, moss and sea green, soft white, with sparing warm accents in orange, red and cobalt. Colour is translucent and stackable in tidy ranges. Minimal ornament, tiny discreet lettering and a small lowercase i-like maker mark. Quiet, functional and nature-minded.'),
('Anglepoise','Europe','1930s','lighting','In the style of Anglepoise, technical, balanced and flexible engineering shown honestly. Slender jointed members, exposed coiled springs and small pivots make a lean, angular, skeletal geometry, finished in crisp, tidy, engineered details. Enamelled and powder-coated metal in jet black, cream, pale grey, signal red, soft teal and mustard sits beside polished brass, chrome and brushed steel. Surfaces are smooth, satin and slightly industrial, with tidy rivets and neatly turned details. Lettering is slim, simple and technical, like a drawing label. Inspired by technical drawing, functional British modernism, precise, witty and understated.'),
('Liberty','Europe','1890s-1900s','textiles','In the style of Liberty, English Aesthetic Movement and Arts and Crafts design with fine, silky, soft-handed cotton lawn and silk. Dense, small-scale floral prints of tiny ditsy blossoms, paisley, peacock feathers, curling tendrils and Japanese-inspired motifs are packed tightly, with hand-drawn irregularity. Palette is rich and slightly dusty, with peacock blue, plum, damson, sage, mustard, coral, rose pink and deep teal, often on dark or cream grounds. Colours are layered, blended and watercolour-soft. Lettering is Art Nouveau serif or flowing script. A refined, romantic, bohemian handcrafted feel with a delicate drape.'),
('Morris and Co','Europe','1860s-1900s','textiles','In the style of Morris and Co, English Arts and Crafts pattern with dense, flat, intertwined foliage, acanthus leaves, willow boughs, pomegranates, tulips and small birds. Designs are symmetrical, rhythmic and repeating, with curving stems that flow in all directions and leave no empty ground. Palette is natural, earthy and slightly muted, with indigo, moss and sage green, madder red, mustard, cream, russet and deep forest tones. Outlines are crisp and hand-drawn, as in woodblock printing, with a flat tapestry-like depth. Lettering is Gothic or medieval inspired. Handcrafted, rich, nature-loving and timeless, rooted in medieval craft.'),
('Pyrex','North America','1950s-70s','homeware','In the style of Pyrex, American mid-century domestic design in glossy glass and creamy opal milk glass. Rounded, plump forms in tidy graduated sets, with smooth, seamless, shiny surfaces. Sunny, saturated colours of turquoise, aqua, primary red, buttercup yellow, avocado green, burnt orange and pink, in flat solid fields. Printed patterns repeat in white or contrasting colours, with snowflakes, daisies, gooseberries, butterflies, stripes, flowers and atomic starbursts, along with retro gingham checks. Lettering is bold, rounded, friendly and slightly retro, in clean sans-serif or script. Cheerful, nostalgic, optimistic and thoroughly wholesome.'),
('Tupperware','North America','1950s-70s','homeware','In the style of Tupperware, cheerful domestic order in translucent, slightly frosted material with a matte waxy finish. Soft rounded corners, gentle stackable shapes and smooth, seamless moulded surfaces. Palette is the bright and pastel mid-century kitchen with harvest orange, avocado green, mustard yellow, sky blue, pink, mint and white, in solid colours or lightly see-through tints. Edges are thick, soft and clean, with simple raised ribbing or concentric rings as the only ornament. Lettering is simple, rounded, friendly sans-serif or a bubbly script. A tidy, modular, practical, optimistic, family-friendly look.'),
('Chevrolet','North America','1950s','cars','In the style of Chevrolet, cheerful, optimistic diner-era American design. Bright chrome with bullet shapes, sharply pointed tapering forms, sweeping side flashes and two-tone lacquer. Palette is turquoise, coral, cream, sky blue, cherry red and ivory, with glossy metallic paint and polished steel highlights. Surfaces are smooth, curvy and streamlined, with jet-inspired forms and wide crosshatch mesh patterns. The emblem is a horizontal, slanted bowtie in gold, blue, red or chrome, often with a thin outline. Lettering is chrome script in flowing, looping letters, joined with bold capitals. Playful, confident, nostalgic and aspirational.'),
]
